From: UniXNU contributors
Subject: [PATCH] k60: force-load the PongWifi kernel archive

The WiFi port builds libPongWifiNative.a but nothing links it. 0009 produces the
archive and the PongWifi sources expect their classes to be present in the
kernel, so without a force_load the archive is inert: the driver compiles, the
symbols exist on disk, and the kernel has none of them.

This adds the archive the same way every other probe archive is added - a
force_load entry plus a dependency so make relinks when the archive changes. The
gate is XNU_PONG_WIFI, which defaults to 0, so a tree that has not built the
archive still links.

The kernel is linked from one of two mutually exclusive archive sets.
KERNEL_EXTRA_ARCHIVES belongs to the CONFIG_XNU_SOURCE_CORECRYPTO14 branch; the
mondrian defconfig leaves that unset (the key is present twice, "y" first and
"n" last, and the parser keeps the last one), so the kernel actually links
through PLATFORM_ARCHIVES.  Adding the archive to only one set silently yields a
kernel without the driver, which is what the first version of this patch did.
Both branches carry it.

--- a/scripts/build-xnu-4k-baseline.sh
+++ b/scripts/build-xnu-4k-baseline.sh
@@ -919,6 +919,12 @@
     KERNEL_EXTRA_ARCHIVES="$KERNEL_EXTRA_ARCHIVES -Wl,-force_load,$CONSTANT_UPLOADS_ARCHIVE"
     KERNEL_ARCHIVE_DEPENDENCIES="$KERNEL_ARCHIVE_DEPENDENCIES $CONSTANT_UPLOADS_ARCHIVE"
   fi
+  if [ "${XNU_PONG_WIFI:-0}" = 1 ]; then
+    PONG_WIFI_ARCHIVE=${XNU_PONG_WIFI_ARCHIVE:-$ROOT/build/pong-wifi/libPongWifiNative.a}
+    test -f "$PONG_WIFI_ARCHIVE"
+    KERNEL_EXTRA_ARCHIVES="$KERNEL_EXTRA_ARCHIVES -Wl,-force_load,$PONG_WIFI_ARCHIVE"
+    KERNEL_ARCHIVE_DEPENDENCIES="$KERNEL_ARCHIVE_DEPENDENCIES $PONG_WIFI_ARCHIVE"
+  fi
   if [ "${XNU_ARMVIRT_PLATFORM:-0}" = 1 ]; then
     ARMVIRT_ARCHIVE=$ROOT/build/armvirt-platform/libArmVirtPlatform.a
     test -f "$ARMVIRT_ARCHIVE"
@@ -1134,6 +1140,12 @@
     PLATFORM_ARCHIVES="$PLATFORM_ARCHIVES -Wl,-force_load,$UFS_ARCHIVE"
     PLATFORM_DEPENDENCIES="$PLATFORM_DEPENDENCIES $UFS_ARCHIVE"
   fi
+  if [ "${XNU_PONG_WIFI:-0}" = 1 ]; then
+    PONG_WIFI_ARCHIVE=${XNU_PONG_WIFI_ARCHIVE:-$ROOT/build/pong-wifi/libPongWifiNative.a}
+    test -f "$PONG_WIFI_ARCHIVE"
+    PLATFORM_ARCHIVES="$PLATFORM_ARCHIVES -Wl,-force_load,$PONG_WIFI_ARCHIVE"
+    PLATFORM_DEPENDENCIES="$PLATFORM_DEPENDENCIES $PONG_WIFI_ARCHIVE"
+  fi
   if [ "$NATIVE_RAM_BLOCK" = 1 ]; then
     RAM_BLOCK_ARCHIVE=$ROOT/build/native-ram-block/libNativeRamBlock.a
     RAM_BLOCK_OBJECT=$ROOT/build/native-ram-block/NativeRamBlock.o
